                <pb facs="1165" n="1041" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg1041"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/157: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Special Mission at
                        Lausanne</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-20T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 20,
                                1922—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Your telegram no. 1 of November 19. There is no objection to your having
                    informal preliminary conversations, at your discretion, <pb facs="1166" n="1042"
                        xml:id="pg1042"/> with Turks or any others. You should, of course, keep in
                    mind that you are not authorized to make any commitments except on instructions
                    from the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
